[] a owl:Axiom ;
    owl:annotatedProperty rdf:type ;
    owl:annotatedSource ns1:EMMO_08cb807c_e626_447b_863f_e2835540e918 ;
    owl:annotatedTarget ns1:EMMO_e7aac247_31d6_4b2e_9fd2_e842b1b7ccac ;
    ns1:conceptualisation """This axiom reflects the fact the the universe is causally self-connected. In fact, a  non causally connected universe would have been the sum of causally independend sub-universes, without any knowledge of others.
This axiom may be seen as Ockam's razor applied to causality."""@en .

